                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Switching to gamepad mode is exactly the same as voluntarily crashing the game. Doing so locks out all input from anything BUT the gamepad, so if for some reason gamepad doesn't work (more on that later) you can't use the KB+M to switch back. There's no choice but to Alt+4 the game. \n\nDoes not support non-xinput controllers, does not respond to x360ce. Unless you've got an official xinput device? No gamepad for you. Also, does not support keyboard-only play like a lot of classic dual stick shooters did, so if you're on the go and want to play on your laptop, you're screwed. In fact, there's no control remapping at all.\n\nGiven that I was hoping to play this on my TV and relax on my couch, KB+M wasn't an option. Guess I'm not playing this at all. At least it was free...",
